        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/the-world-deserves-food-sovereignty-and-more-secured-food-access-for-everybody",
        "orario": "13:57",
        "timestamp": 1777550220,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'The world deserves food sovereignty and more secured food access for everybody' Americas Issued on: 30/04/2026 - 13:57 Modified: 30/04/2026 - 14:09 As geopolitical instability exposes the deep entanglement between energy, food systems, and global security, Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Delphine Lévi Alvarès, Petrochemicals Campaign Manager at the Center for International Environmental Law (CIEL). Joining us from a high-level summit in Colombia, Ms. Alvarès says we've reached a critical juncture that requires steadfast action. The on-going conflict and instability in the Middle East, she argues, is less an “opportunity” than a moral and systemic reckoning: “a stark reminder that we have to decouple our economies from fossil fuels.” 30/04/2026 Americas US: Hegseth under fire in Congress over Iran war as diplomacy stalls 30/04/2026 Americas US: Supreme Court weakens voting rigths act 30/04/2026 Americas Putin, in call with Trump, put forward ideas on Iran, Kremlin says 29/04/2026 Americas United States: Limited-edition Trump passport unveiled 🇺🇸 29/04/2026 Americas King Charles’s US visit ‘about future generations, not just the current administration’ 29/04/2026 UK King Charles III in the US : 'If it wasn't for us, you'd be speaking French' 29/04/2026 Americas From the oceans into our bodies: Plastic pollution 'associated with obesity and dementia' 29/04/2026 Environment US 'used to' school shootings: Gun violence 'inevitably turned to the political arena as well' 27/04/2026 Americas"
